Using the distance formula with the **original coordinates**:

\[
\begin{aligned}
\Delta x &= (-4)-(-11)=7,\\[4pt]
\Delta y &= (-5)-12=-17.
\end{aligned}
\]

Then

\[
\text{distance}=\sqrt{(\Delta x)^2+(\Delta y)^2}
  =\sqrt{7^2+(-17)^2}
  =\sqrt{49+289}
  =\sqrt{338}\approx 18.38.
\]

So the correct distance between \((-11,12)\) and \((-4,-5)\) is about **18.4 units**.

