   = \frac{-9+16}{-15+9}
   = \frac{7}{-6}
   = -\frac{7}{6}.
\]

So the line through \((-9,-16)\) and \((-15,-9)\) has a slope of \(-7/6\). I’ll be more careful with the subtraction next time!

